# Where background work lives

Phase 1 ships no Celery (it is not a pinned dependency). Anything that must
eventually happen because a write happened goes through the outbox table
(`apps.core.models.OutboxEvent`, written in the same transaction as the
write) and is dispatched by:

    python manage.py dispatch_outbox

run on a scheduler (cron / host timer). `apps.core.services.dispatch_batch`
is the single implementation of claiming (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED + optimistic
attempts claim) and retry/backoff.

## When Celery lands

Add `celery` to requirements, create `config/celery.py` with the standard
Django integration, and register ONE task per queue concern, each a thin
wrapper:

    @shared_task
    def dispatch_outbox_batch():
        dispatch_batch()

Never reimplement claiming inside a task — the dispatcher above is the only
claiming logic, so the management command and the workers stay interchangeable.
